# Large per-judge raw severity table (13 MB, regeneratable via
# scripts/compute_inter_judge_agreement.py)
tables/inter_judge_raw.csv

# The same two tables again, one copy per decomposition condition (~15 MB).
# Same rationale as above: bulky, purely derived, and regeneratable with
#   scripts/compute_inter_judge_agreement.py --personas <condition> \
#       --tables-dir tables/decomposition/alpha_<condition>
#   scripts/compute_judge_artifact_controls.py --personas ... \
#       --output-dir tables/decomposition
# The small summary tables built from them (alpha_by_condition.md,
# judge_artifact_controls.md, judge_blinding_check.csv) ARE committed.
tables/decomposition/alpha_*/inter_judge_raw.csv
tables/decomposition/response_disclosure_rates.csv

# Multi-label scoring datasets (7 MB). They embed archived model responses, and
# `logs/` is ignored above for exactly that reason -- responses are not published
# from this repo. Regeneratable byte-for-byte via
# scripts/build_discriminant_multilabel_dataset.py, and their sha256s are
# recorded in data/discriminant/manifest.json, which IS committed.
data/discriminant/multilabel_*.jsonl

# --- Stripped from history 2026-07-26; kept on disk, never published ---------
#
# Internal strategy documents for a paper under anonymous review. They quote
# confidential peer-review text verbatim with per-reviewer attribution, and
# carry rebuttal framing. This repo is mirrored to anonymous.4open.science with
# substring-only redaction, which would scrub the names and leave the strategy
# intact for the reviewers to read.
# Anchored to the repo root: a bare filename would match at any depth, and
# docs/discriminant_validity_design.md is the redacted public version that four
# modules cite.
/humanebench_aaai27_revision_plan.md
/adversarial-conditions.md
/DECOMP_HANDOFF.md
/discriminant_validity_design.md

# Working results and reconciliation notes. Numbers reach the repo through
# tables/; the prose write-ups stay local.
/results/

